    "title": "Kristin Cavallari slips back into her controversial 'Laguna Beach' minidress for reunion episode",
    "text": "Kristin Cavallari hit the red carpet at the “Laguna Beach” reunion premiere in a white strapless minidress — recreating a look from the show’s pilot episode. Todd Williamson/JanuaryImages / BACKGRID Two decades later and Kristin Cavallari’s still the girl in white. The former “Laguna Beach” star, 39, wore a white strapless minidress and a black choker to Thursday night’s premiere event for “The Reunion: Laguna Beach” in a deliberate callback to the MTV show’s very first episode. In the 2004 pilot, “A Black & White Affair,” co-star Lo Bosworth dismissed white dresses as “trashy and tacky” while getting ready for a black-and-white-themed party. A teenage Cavallari showed up in white anyway, prompting Lauren Conrad to quip, “I like how we’re all wearing black and Kristin’s wearing white. How ironic” — a line that established the pair as rivals and set the tone for Cavallari’s’ role as the show’s resident rule-breaker. In the original episode, a teenage Cavallari was the only girl to wear white to a black-and-white party, a move then-rival Lauren Conrad called “ironic.” MTV The 39-year-old paired the look with a black choker from her jewelry line, Uncommon James. Todd Williamson/JanuaryImages / BACKGRID Cavallari explained her outfit choice on Instagram Stories before the event at Shutters On The Beach in Santa Monica, Calif., calling the dress an “elevated” take on the original. kristincavallari/Instagram Cavallari leaned into the moment, explaining her outfit choice on her brand Uncommon James’ Instagram Stories before hitting the red carpet at Shutters On The Beach in Santa Monica, Calif. “Tonight I was like, I have to wear a white dress, and it has to be similar. So it’s like an elevated dress from the original,” she said. She accessorized with the Uncommon James Laguna black choker ($45), beige lace-up sandals and a black clutch. “Someone said Laguna Beach is back….and that means the black choker is too,” she wrote on Instagram. This time around, Cavallari wasn’t alone in her color choice: co-stars Lauren Conrad and Morgan Smith (née Olsen) also wore white dresses to the premiere. Shop ’til you drop with Post Wanted Save time and money with the latest deals, discounts, trends, reviews and more. Thanks for signing up! Cavallari and Conrad have since mended bridges, and this time around, both wore white. Todd Williamson/JanuaryImages / BACKGRID “The Reunion: Laguna Beach” brings the original cast together for the first time in 20 years. FilmMagic Cavallari has said that filming the reunion was “very therapeutic.” MTV The premiere celebrated “The Reunion: Laguna Beach,” a two-hour Roku special premiering April 10 that brings the original cast — including Stephen Colletti, Bosworth and Talan Torriero — together on screen for the first time in 20 years. Cavallari, Conrad and Colletti also serve as executive producers. In the reunion’s trailer, which dropped earlier this week, Cavallari addresses her former rival directly. “We have never had a conversation on camera just the two of us. Are you ready?” she asks Conrad. The mom of three has said filming was “very therapeutic” and that she and Conrad are now friends. “Everyone can put away their team Lauren and team Kristin shirts now,” she wrote on Instagram last year. “Laguna Beach: The Real Orange County” debuted on MTV in September 2004 and ran for three seasons. Inspired by the teen drama “The O.C.,” the series followed a group of teens in the wealthy coastal California town and launched Conrad, Cavallari and Colletti into stardom — along with spin-offs “The Hills” and “The City.”",
